  "description": "The 126 superintendent registrars' districts of the Irish Free State at the census of 26 Apr 1936, the registration areas for births, deaths and marriages. Table 10 of the census report prints them county by county under the names of the former Poor Law Unions, each within one county. Each is the union of its dispensary districts on Dispensary Districts 26 Apr 1936, with the same sources, DED map and grades. It carries the number of DEDs and dispensary districts it holds and their combined population; the district holding a county borough (Dublin, Cork, Limerick, Waterford) takes in the city on the map, but its population leaves the city out.",
